<Article h1={"Privacy and your choices"} subtitle={"You can use the free tools without an account or analytics consent."} crumbs={[{"name":"Privacy"}]} title="Privacy & Analytics Choices | DeadHangs" description="How DeadHangs handles analytics choices, local training logs, Google sign-in, optional cloud sync, payments, email signup and affiliate links.">
<div class="article-body"><p>Updated 8 November 2026. DeadHangs is operated by ND Media Ltd. Contact <a href="mailto:hello@sunnypatel.co.uk">hello@sunnypatel.co.uk</a> about this page or a data request.</p><h2>Training log, goal and calculator</h2><p>The training log stores dates, hold times, assistance types, set counts and any setup you record (bar, grip, chalk and added load), plus an optional body weight converted to kg, in this browser's local storage when you choose to save an entry. A saved goal and session settings are stored separately in this browser only when you choose Save plan. The timer does not upload these entries or settings. If you choose to sync entries from your account page, those entries are copied to your cloud log. Training entries and account details are never sent by us to Google Analytics. Other people using the same browser profile may be able to see them. The log provides export, individual deletion and clear-all controls.</p><p>Clearing site data or switching browser profiles can remove access to your log. The free device log has no automatic backup. Optional Pro cloud sync is managed separately from your account page; signing in alone does not upload entries. The calculator uses your entries on the current page. Choosing Review this goal in the timer keeps your target and hold in this browser only long enough to open the setup tool. It does not save a plan or log entry. Choosing a starter session on the dead hang time by age card opens the timer with that session's settings in the link, without your hold time. Nothing starts or saves until you choose to.</p><h2>Google sign-in and your account</h2><p>Google sign-in gives DeadHangs your name, email address, whether that email is verified, and a Google account identifier. We use these details to create your account, recognise you on another device and provide the account features you request. We do not receive your Google password, read your Gmail or subscribe you to marketing emails. We do not keep Google's profile picture or access, refresh or ID tokens.</p><p>Cloudflare D1 stores your account and cloud log. Essential, secure cookies keep you signed in and protect the sign-in process. A session normally lasts up to 30 days and can refresh as you use the account. Sign out on a shared device; use Sign out all devices in your account to revoke existing sessions. These essential cookies work independently of analytics consent.</p><h2>Optional cloud training log</h2><p>Pro lets you copy saved training entries into your account and retrieve them on another device. Sync happens only when you choose a sync action. A merge can include dates, hold times, assistance, sets, setup and optional body weight already saved in this browser. Check that device entries belong to you before importing them. Your separately saved timer settings and goal are not synced.</p><p>Your account page shows the stored log and offers export, clear-cloud-log and account-deletion controls. Cloud log entries remain available to export or delete after Pro ends. We keep them while your account exists unless you clear them. Account deletion removes the account, sign-in sessions and cloud log from the active application database. Cloudflare recovery copies may retain prior data for their configured recovery period. Deleting an account does not clear training entries stored on other devices; use each device's local controls for those.</p><h2>Payments</h2><p>When paid checkout is available, Stripe processes your subscription payment and stores payment details. DeadHangs stores Stripe customer and subscription references, the selected plan, payment status and paid-through date to manage access. Card numbers are not stored in our application. Account deletion must stop any continuing subscription before the account is removed. Payment records may remain with Stripe where needed for accounting, refunds or legal obligations. <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">Stripe privacy policy</a>.</p><h2>Offline use</h2><p>Your browser keeps a copy of the timer page and its files so the timer works without a connection. This copy holds site files only, not your log. Sign-in, account management and cloud sync require a connection; account and payment responses are not stored by the offline cache. Clearing site data removes it.</p><h2>Analytics</h2><p>Google Analytics loads only after you accept analytics on this site. It is not loaded on account or Pro pages. It measures visits, page activity and tagged equipment-link clicks. Training-tool custom measurements use only a page pathname, the tool's placement on the site, the name of the feature used (for example "max test started" or "bar card printed"), where relevant the timer mode, the starter session you picked (Level 1, 2 or 3) and whether a save was the first training session or first test hold in this browser's log. They do not include your recorded hold times, targets, ages, setups, assistance, body weight, dates, log IDs, form values or full URLs. To show how visitors find the site, Google Analytics receives the website you came from as its domain only (for example google.com), never that page's address or search words, and campaign labels from a link (utm_source, utm_medium and utm_campaign) only when they match a fixed public allowlist. Visits between pages of this site are not counted as arrivals from another website. Google may process online identifiers and technical data according to its own policies. Google Analytics data is not anonymous.</p><p>You can change your choice below or in the footer. Declining prevents further measurement through this site's configured Google Analytics tag and clears its first-party analytics cookies where accessible. It does not delete data already processed by Google.</p><button type="button" class="dh-btn" data-open-consent>Change analytics choice</button><p><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy policy</a>.</p><h2>Optional email signup</h2><p>An email signup form sends your email address to Brevo to manage the subscription. The signup also records a signup date and email-sequence status. Training-log entries are not attached. Use the unsubscribe link in a received message or contact us to request removal.</p><p>The printable session planner is available directly without subscribing. A successful signup message confirms registration but not delivery to your inbox. <a href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/">Brevo privacy policy</a>.</p><h2>Contact messages</h2><p>The contact link opens your mail app. A message you send gives us its content and the sender details from your email service. We use them to respond. Include only information needed for your inquiry.</p><h2>Affiliate links</h2><p>Clearly marked Amazon links take you to Amazon, which may send you to your local Amazon store. Amazon may use its own cookies and process information under its policies after you visit. As an Amazon Associate, DeadHangs.com earns from qualifying purchases.</p><h2>Hosting</h2><p>Cloudflare serves this site and may process request information for delivery, reliability and security. This is separate from optional Google Analytics.</p><p><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.</p><h2>Requests and retention</h2><p>Delete local training entries with the controls in the tool. Export or delete your cloud log and account from the account page. We use account and payment information to provide the service you request and protect access; optional analytics uses your consent. Contact us about information sent by email or subscription forms. We will respond to applicable access, correction, deletion or objection requests. Exact analytics retention is controlled in the Google Analytics account and is not stated here without verification.</p></div></Article>
